  <ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock id="Tag476" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;1) None&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;2) None&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;3) As of January 1, 2025, 223 miles of our Mississippi pipeline system were indefinitely idled. As of March 31, 2025, management does not foresee any future use in providing common carrier pipeline service on these segments and they have no useful value. As such, the related&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;assets were retired from service during Q1 2025, which resulted in a reduction of both our Carrier Property and Accrued Depreciation - Carrier Property during the period.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;4) None&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;5 Not Applicable&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock>
  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="Tag477" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Genesis Pipeline USA, LP owns and operates a network of crude oil pipeline assets concentrated in Louisiana, Alabama, Florida, and Mississippi, focused on gathering or transporting crude oil production&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;and delivering to local refineries. Genesis also owns tanks and other pipeline related assets that service pipeline operations. The accompanying consolidated financial statements are presented in&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;accordance with the Uniform System of Accounts prescribed by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC). The preparation of financial statements requires us to make estimates and assumptions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;that affect the reported amounts of assets and liabilities and disclosure of contingent assets and liabilities at the date of the financial statements and the reported amounts of revenues and expenses during&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;the reporting period.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As of January 1, 2025, 223 miles of our Mississippi pipeline system were indefinitely idled. As of March 31, 2025, management does not foresee any future use in providing common carrier pipeline service on these segments and they have no useful value. As such, the related&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;assets were retired from service during Q1 2025, which resulted in a reduction of both our Carrier Property and Accrued Depreciation - Carrier Property during the period.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
